From eacb1d57db7f949b01d37411ba91287904f0184c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 01:54:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 37/38] hir_conv: don't abort when eager constant evaluation
 reaches `panic!()`

mrustc evaluates every constant, including associated constants of
(lifetime-)generic impls, during the early "Constant Evaluate" pass.
rustc only evaluates an associated constant when something uses it, and
zerocopy 0.7 relies on that: `<cell::Ref<[u8]> as ByteSlice>::
INTO_REF_INTO_MUT_ARE_SOUND` is a deliberate `panic!()` so that only a
program calling `Ref::into_ref`/`into_mut` with a `cell::Ref` fails to
compile. Under mrustc the eager pass hit the panic and died with
"MIR TODO: panic in constant evaluation" for every zerocopy user.

Introduce `ConstEvalPanic` (a `Defer`) thrown when the evaluator calls the
`panic_impl` hook. The eager pass then leaves the constant unevaluated
like any other deferred constant, and if a monomorphised use does need
the value, Trans Monomorph reports "Constant evaluation panicked while
evaluating <path>" instead of crashing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
